2. Primary LCDM on stack P, data covariance only: chi2 35.25 / 15 with all bins; 17.57 / 13 without the 1.04 and 1.38 Mpc bins (p 0.174). POST-HOC: dropping bins is not a validation.

3. E (stack P) at 1.82 / 1.38 / 1.04 / 0.78 Mpc: nonlinear 0.601 / 0.400 / 0.726 / 1.426; CFG502 linear 0.471 / 0.470 / 0.855 / 1.467. The nonlinear term raises E beyond ~1.6 Mpc but LOWERS it at 1.0-1.4 Mpc: with a sharp exclusion at r_ta, the extra mass just outside r_ta projects to a negative Delta Sigma just inside it.
